WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.850
- You know, here's the thing.

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:07.310
In July, it was two years
since I've had a drink,

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:09.810
because, two years.
- Oh!

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:14.050
- Because as we said, I don't
think I'm gonna have grandkids

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:16.930
for many, many years and when they come,

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:21.160
I'll probably be about 75,
and so I need my brain.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:24.640
I don't want to be that drooling
grandmother in the corner,

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.320
you know, that you have to go
kiss and then run away from.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:28.960
I want to be at an active level, you know.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.700
So I haven't been drinking
to preserve my brain, right?

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.533
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:36.330
- However, it doesn't seem
to have helped that much,

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.710
because...
(laughing)

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:43.000
the other night, I get a
text from my youngest son

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.290
and he says, "Well, happy
birthday to me, I guess."

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:49.690
And I realized--

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.170
- My mother did this once!

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:53.860
- And not only was it his birthday,

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:56.495
it was his 21st birthday.

00:00:56.495 --> 00:00:59.010
- Oh no!
(Patricia laughs)

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.720
- I'm at the top of the stairs.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.703
This was before the pandemic,
so he was still at school.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.778
(laughing) I yelled
down the stairs, "Dave!

00:01:06.778 --> 00:01:09.500
"We forgot Dan's birthday!"

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.640
Dave was like, "Oh my God."

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:15.640
So I, and it's 21st birthday,
so I felt so, so bad...

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:20.280
That I started texting every
celebrity friend that I had

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.460
and I gave them Dan's phone number.

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:28.727
And I said, "Please,
will you text my son Dan?

00:01:28.727 --> 00:01:30.797
"It's his 21st birthday, I forgot.

00:01:30.797 --> 00:01:32.677
"Please just text him,
wish him happy birthday.

00:01:32.677 --> 00:01:35.010
"Tell him I'm a terrible parent."

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:37.630
And Dan was very impressed.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:40.880
First of all, his roommates
at college were very impressed

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:44.270
that Ashley Tisdale was texting him, so--

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.110
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh, she's so nice!

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:48.270
- So nice, and she was having
a conversation with him.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:51.400
She told me later, her husband
said, "Who are you texting?"

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.215
And she said, "A bunch of college boys."

00:01:53.215 --> 00:01:54.310
(laughing)

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:59.260
But the best one was Ray
Romano sent me a video,

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:01.390
or sent Dan a video and
then he sent it to me.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:04.593
And it's really funny what
he said, I think you have it.

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:08.263
- Hey Dan, I know it's a little noisy.

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:12.130
I understand it's your 21st birthday,

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:13.683
according to my calendar.

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:19.090
I guess your parents don't have
the same calendar than I do,

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:22.553
but I keep track of things,
so happy 21st birthday.

